SnarkyCtl for Debian and Ubuntu
================================

This package deliberately installs an inactive, unconfigured service.
Installation does not alter VPN, WireGuard, routing, DNS, or firewall state.

Configuration examples are installed under:

  /usr/share/snarkyctl/examples/

Follow the installation guide in the project repository before enabling any units. In
particular, create the configuration, authentication file, and TLS identity, then run:

  sudo snarkyctl preflight

After preflight succeeds, explicitly enable and start the socket and web unit:

  sudo systemctl enable --now snarkyctl-control.socket
  sudo systemctl enable --now snarkyctl-web.service

The privileged service is socket-activated. Do not start
snarkyctl-control.service directly.
